'''Pablo Picasso''' (1881–1973) was a Spanish painter, sculptor, and printmaker who co-founded the Cubist movement. He was born in [[Málaga]] and spent most of his working life in France.

NeoWiki exports this page's structured data through the [[Mapping:EDM|EDM]] and [[Mapping:CIDOC-CRM|CIDOC CRM]] mappings. In EDM, his birth date and place stay properties of the agent. The CIDOC CRM mapping creates an E67 Birth in Málaga, with the date on an E52 Time-Span. You can download both exports from the [[RDF and ontology mappings]] page.
